      "path": ".claude/scripts/with-browser-lock.sh",
      "content": "Guard reclamation can remove a live taker's guard and reintroduce the double-takeover race. For example, two waiters observe an expired guard; one removes it and a taker acquires a replacement, then the delayed second waiter executes rmdir against that replacement. Another taker can now enter while the first is between its PID comparison and rm, allowing it to delete a newly acquired lock. Also, elapsed time alone does not prove the guard owner has died. Use a takeover synchronization mechanism whose ownership/recovery cannot be invalidated by a delayed waiter; unconditional age-based rmdir does not preserve mutual exclusion.",
      "existing_code": "    gage=$(( $(date +%s) - $(stat -f %m \"$guard\" 2\u003e/dev/null || date +%s) ))\n    (( gage \u003e 10 )) \u0026\u0026 rmdir \"$guard\" 2\u003e/dev/null",
